{"created": "2026-10-17T23:12:45.847488+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-17T23:12:46.416053+00:00", "id": 23443301, "conceptrecid": "23443300", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23443301", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23443300", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23443301", "metadata": {"title": "Polynomial compatibility on the Boolean cube from disjoint-support separators", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23443301", "publication_date": "2026-10-17", "description": "<p>A complete affirmative deduction for Austrin's exact two-polynomial question, OWR 9/2025 printed p. 445 (30006210 / OWR-14299088-012). For every positive n,d and nonzero real multilinear f,g of degree at most d on the uniform sign cube, all full-norm relative coordinate influences at most 1/(4096d^8) guarantee a common nonzero vertex. Disjoint supports force maximum relative influence at least1/(1024d^8). The denominator includes the constant Fourier coefficient; arbitrary common zeros are allowed. Constants/exponent are not claimed optimal. General distribution formulations, other groups/measures and approximate supports are outside the asserted theorem.</p><p>This four-page note is an explicit target-specific application of the established Li-Li-Li-Liu 2026 disjoint-support separator and O'Donnell-Saks-Schramm-Servedio 2005 section3.3 Eq(6) real covariance inequality, with the classical Markov/Bernoulli presentation credited to Kothari and coauthors. Neither the separator nor covariance inequality is claimed new. The complete square-density conversion and extracted depth 16d^4 are supplied.</p><p>Extensive bounded primary priority audits found no earlier recorded complete target-specific deduction in the bodies inspected. They do not certify novelty, first discovery/publication or global current openness. The full ePrint 2022/218 and full 2023/570 followup were inaccessible; the official CRYPTO 2022 conference version was read and separately pinned. Other historical coverage and procedural-independence limits are documented. Dates and negative searches do not certify firstness or causal independence.</p><p>The source archive preserves all ten original PR artifacts, three distinct mathematical audits, three priority approaches, root checks, and a portable offline standard-library verification runner. Four exact integer/rational programs run in ordinary and optimized modes with all mathematical fields compared exactly and forty actual incorrect-result failures. Finite checks supplement the universal proof; they are not arbitrary-dimensional enumeration or formal proof certificates. Third-party source bodies are excluded.</p><p>AI tools were used extensively in proof development, writing, computation, reproduction, literature research and adversarial verification. This note and package are unrefereed. Internal AI-assisted reviews do not constitute external human peer review, journal acceptance or formal proof-assistant certification.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Kriebel, Alec", "affiliation": "Independent researcher", "orcid": "0009-0001-9320-500X"}], "keywords": ["Boolean cube", "polynomial compatibility", "relative influence", "multilinear polynomials", "disjoint supports", "OSSS inequality", "decision trees"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.4171/OWR/2025/9", "relation": "references", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.1007/978-3-031-15979-4_6", "relation": "references", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.03824v1", "relation": "references", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.08727v3", "relation": "references", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "10.1109/SFCS.2005.34", "relation": "references", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/cs/0508071v1", "relation": "references", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/1141", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "scheme": "url"}], "version": "1.0.0", "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23443300"}}]}}, "title": "Polynomial compatibility on the Boolean cube from disjoint-support separators", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23443301", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23443301", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23443301?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23443301", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23443301", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23443301", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23443301/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23443300", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23443300", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23443300", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23443300", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23443301/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23443301/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23443301/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23443301/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23443301:polynomial-compatibility.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23443301:polynomial-compatibility.pdf/full/%5E50,/0/default.jpg", "100": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23443301:polynomial-compatibility.pdf/full/%5E100,/0/default.jpg", "250": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23443301:polynomial-compatibility.pdf/full/%5E250,/0/default.jpg", "750": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23443301:polynomial-compatibility.pdf/full/%5E750,/0/default.jpg", "1200": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23443301:polynomial-compatibility.pdf/full/%5E1200,/0/default.jpg"}, "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23443301/versions/latest", "latest_html": "h